{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0603"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c051): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c051.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0603"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge art/architecture","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/art__architecture.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",50],["-","Five"],["+","Six"],["=",915],["+","Sometimes a building's nickname is a joke. Bonn's former high-rise for members of parliament, designed by Egon Eiermann and completed in 1969, rises about 115 metres over the Rhine and was built on the initiative of the President of the Bundestag Eugen Gerstenmaier. Because he was a notably short man, the tallest building in the capital was soon called the „Langer Eugen“ – “Long Eugene”. Since 2006 it has been the heart of the UN Campus in Bonn.\n\n"],["=",149],["+","\n| Langer Eugen | Eugen Gerstenmaier, President of the Bundestag | former MPs' high-rise in Bonn |"],["=",56]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",50],["-","Fünf"],["+","Sechs"],["=",863],["+","Manchmal ist der Spitzname eines Gebäudes ein Scherz. Das frühere Abgeordnetenhochhaus in Bonn, von Egon Eiermann entworfen und 1969 fertiggestellt, ragt rund 115 Meter über den Rhein und entstand auf Betreiben von Bundestagspräsident Eugen Gerstenmaier. Weil er auffallend klein war, hieß das höchste Gebäude der Hauptstadt bald der „Lange Eugen“. Seit 2006 ist es das Herz des UN-Campus in Bonn.\n\n"],["=",141],["+","\n| Langer Eugen | Bundestagspräsident Eugen Gerstenmaier | früheres Abgeordnetenhochhaus in Bonn |"],["=",54]]}]},
